WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.303
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.171
My name is Jimmy Fallon,
and I am going to use

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:09.109
a kind of teleprompter
right now.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.311
And I'll take a picture
of what I'm seeing

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.512
so you know what I'm seeing,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.881
just so we can try to get
through the monologue.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.382
We'll do the monologue
like this.

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:19.652
But, anyways, this is our show.
Welcome. We have a great show.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.121
Alex Rodriguez is here, "A-Rod,"
Rhett and Link,

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.455
music from Tones and I.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:26.826
But, first, let's get to some
jokes here, everybody.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.794
Well, I'm so excited about
tonight's show

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.463
because we are filming
the entire thing

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.532
from Roger Goodell's basement.

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.135
That's right -- tonight was
night one of the NFL Draft,

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:37.771
and this year,
the commissioner announced

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.205
the picks from his basement.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.006
And, of course,
right when he started talking,

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:42.842
someone started vacuuming.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.678
"Do you have to do that now?"

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.314
Hey!"

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.382
That's right --
tonight was the NFL draft.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.219
You know things are nuts when
the most exciting sports moment

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.288
in six weeks is a guy
in his basement

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:58.391
reading names off an index card.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.960
Yeah, it was a virtual draft,
which got pretty frustrating

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.563
when players would be anxiously
sitting at home and hear,

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.265
"The New England Patriots
select..."

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:11.404
[ Audio cutting out ]

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.706
Congratulations."

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.075
"Who did he say?
Was it me? Was it me?

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.878
Did you --
My phone's not ringing."

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.380
This year's draft was supposed
to take place in Las Vegas,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.551
but the NFL didn't want to put
people's health in danger.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.419
That's how crazy things are.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.621
The NFL is more concerned
about health

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.124
than the mayor of Las Vegas.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.758
That's right -- everyone was
talking about this yesterday.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.127
Anderson Cooper interviewed
the mayor of Las Vegas,

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.063
who wants to reopen the city,

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:40.199
and this image
pretty much sums it up.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.735
Yeah, the mayor wants to open
Las Vegas back up,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.971
and she's even come up with
a few slogans

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.373
that will help encourage
tourists to come back.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:51.710
For example, there's "Vegas --
the stakes just got higher."

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.047
Then there's
"Vegas -- it's a gamble."

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.983
Next, there's "Viva Las Virus."

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:03.155
There's also, "Vegas -- hot
games, cold drinks, dry coughs."

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.959
And, finally, "Vegas, where
'Ocean's Eleven'

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.894
meets COVID-19."

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.628
Well, good luck
to everyone involved.

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:10.763
Listen to this.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.565
I saw that the first-ever
YouTube video

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.234
was posted 15 years ago today.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.735
The first comment was,
"Love it."

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:18.304
The next was, "How cool."

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:22.441
And the third began a
15-year argument over politics.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:23.743
Well, this isn't good.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:26.945
I saw that Chipotle just agreed
to pay $25 million

00:02:26.945 --> 00:02:29.082
in food-safety fines.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:32.552
Ah! Remember the good old days
when the only deadly viruses

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:35.721
were in the lettuce at Chipotle?

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:39.191
I saw that the toy company Ty
has debuted a new Beanie Baby

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:42.161
to raise money for the
coronavirus recovery efforts.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.063
It's a great idea
that's expected to bring in

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:48.067
millions of dollars
in the year 1995.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.068
Check this out.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.536
I heard that tie-dye is becoming

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.872
a big quarantine fashion trend.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.373
It's awkward when
a co-worker asks,

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.808
"Are you wearing tie-dye?",
and you go,

00:02:55.808 --> 00:03:02.881
"No, this is ketchup, mustard,
relish, and Cheeto? Cheeto."

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:05.118
And, finally, I saw that
the coronavirus lockdown

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:08.788
is increasing the demand for
video-game coaches.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:11.257
Wow. If you think people who sit
around playing video games

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.993
all day is out of shape,
imagine their coaches.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.429
That's our monologue, everybody.
Now it's time for "Hashtags."

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.930
♪♪

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.401
-♪ "Hashtags" ♪

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:26.406
♪ "Hashtags" ♪

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.574
-As I said,
we have a great show tonight.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:32.144
He's a superstar, one of the
best athletes of all time.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:35.314
Alex Rodriguez, "A-Rod," is on
the show tonight.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.016
We're going to be talking to him
about some fun stuff

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.884
and we're doing a "Hot Ones."

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:39.919
That's right.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.621
So all you sports fans
out there,

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.622
not only do you get to see one
of your favorites,

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.792
but he's also going to eat
the spiciest wings

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.993
you've ever seen him eat,
and Sean Evans

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.428
is going to help us out
with that.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.130
Also, we have our pals
Rhett and Link,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.665
who I miss so much.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.333
"Good Mythical Morning."

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.869
YouTube superstars
Rhett and Link will be on.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:04:00.139
And we have great, great music
from Tones and I,

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:02.475
who -- Of course,
she sings "Dance Monkey,"

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.276
which was the biggest thing
that we've, I think,

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.412
had on our show, virally.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:10.116
Ooh, I can't even say
"virally" anymore.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:14.053
Popularity-wise?

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.654
Should I start over?
-No.

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:18.324
-Yeah, okay.
I don't know what to say.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:22.361
I don't know -- It's the biggest
thing that we've had

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:25.898
on our show, with like
80 million hits on YouTube.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.701
I don't even know
if they're hits.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.303
Okay.
Let's get right to "Hashtags."

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.538
Here we go.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.841
The hashtag -- This is the game
we play every week.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.308
So if you want to play along,
you can do this.

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:38.911
I will send out a thing
probably on Tuesday

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.447
with a hashtag saying a subject.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.649
Tonight's subject is
"Quarantine Quotes."

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:46.819
Things that you've heard being
under quarantine.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:51.057
So, everyone sent in
their favorite quotes.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.491
We trended number 1 in the U.S.,

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:55.261
so thank you so much for doing
that and playing the game.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.629
We like to do this with you guys
and we appreciate it.

00:04:57.629 --> 00:05:01.034
So, here's the hashtags for
quarantine quotes.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:04.103
First one's from @Jamieboge.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.006
She said, "There is
no longer A.M. or P.M.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:11.143
There is just coffee time
or wine time."

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:14.513
This one's from @Chad0616.

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:17.215
He said, "There should be
an ice-cream truck

00:05:17.215 --> 00:05:19.218
that sells toilet paper."

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.087
That's thinking.
That's a good man.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:24.723
This one's from @thedoots.
Thedoots.

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:26.792
They said, "I'm starting
to get a tan from

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:29.595
checking my refrigerator."

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:35.368
See? It could happen.
This one's from @rbellaruso.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:36.769
She said, "My car is getting

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.173
three weeks to the gallon."

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.942
This one's from @marketingprofb.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.310
He said, "I can't wait to see

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.747
what Instacart is going to
substitute today."

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:53.018
"We don't have yogurt.
Do you want toothpaste?

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:54.420
It looks like yogurt."

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.656
"No, thanks."

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:58.958
This one's from @stratladyk.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.360
She says,
"Now I understand why pets

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.596
try to run out of the house
when the door opens."

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:09.267
These are quarantine quotes.
Now this one's from @Joshrozner.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.770
He said, "20 years from now,
the country will be run

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:15.207
by people who were homeschooled
by day drinkers."

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:19.278
[ Laughs ]

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:23.382
This one's from @Hollynherren.
She said, "I better go.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:27.220
One of my Sims
is getting married."

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.287
You don't want to miss that.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:33.191
That's a big
moment -- milestone.

00:06:33.191 --> 00:06:36.062
This one's from -- I remember
I used to play "Sims."

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.396
Years ago, I was on
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.132
and I was living in my
studio apartment and I had --

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:41.867
You know, my bed was
attached to the kitchen,

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:43.702
was attached the bathroom,
was attached to --

00:06:43.702 --> 00:06:45.838
Everything was in
one room -- studio.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.841
And I was in -- I changed my
closet into a tiny desk,

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.309
a tiny office.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:53.212
Not so many things have changed.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:55.548
And I remember playing
"The Sims,"

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:57.683
and I was making my -- I was
eating a pizza.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.218
I was hunched over,
'cause that's where --

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.286
The desk I built was there.

00:07:01.286 --> 00:07:04.790
And I was eating a pizza and
I was over, like, a paper plate.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:08.260
And I'm making my "Sims"
character run on a treadmill

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.830
'cause he was too overweight.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:16.269
And I was like, "Lose weight!
Lose weight!

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:17.436
Gosh."

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:22.208
Eating a whole pizza
in a closet,

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:24.576
making a video game lose weight.

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:27.380
Alright, here we go.
This one's from @mamabrianne.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.448
She said, "Kids born in 2020

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:33.852
shall be known as
Children of the Quarn."

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:36.755
Children of the Quarn.

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:41.827
This one's from @Jeremypimples.
Come on. Come on.

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:44.763
Jeremy Pimples -- he said,
"Crap, now I can't pretend

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:47.433
I'm not at home when
the doorbell rings."

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:50.870
This one's from @ywilson2330.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.072
She said, "The dumbest thing
I ever purchased?

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:56.275
A 2020 planner."

00:07:56.275 --> 00:08:00.946
What a waste of money, yep.
This one's from @Webhank.

00:08:00.946 --> 00:08:04.049
He said, "I said to my family,
'I can't think of three people

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:06.251
I'd rather be
quarantined with.'

00:08:06.251 --> 00:08:10.523
My 11-year-old
immediately said, 'Oh, I can.'"

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:12.058
Those are our
"Hashtags," everybody.

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:14.727
We have a great show tonight.
Thank you so much for tuning in.

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:17.028
More of the
"Tonight Show: At Home"

00:08:17.028 --> 00:08:18.030
with A-Rod coming up.

